{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-10",
  "title": "Discussion",
  "author": "person:jane-brew:001",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Discussion"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "[https://chatgpt.com/g/g-wbfoUANvp-daria/c/677263d2-49b0-8010-966a-cadf30f61c26](https://chatgpt.com/g/g-wbfoUANvp-daria/c/677263d2-49b0-8010-966a-cadf30f61c26)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "this model feels like a clever twist on the classic “retainer” arrangement, wrapped in shiny subscription packaging. the emphasis on tools like linear, slack, and stripe gives it a streamlined, modern vibe—one that clients who are already used to the design joy model might find both familiar and appealing. but let’s not sugarcoat it: the success here hinges on managing expectations and execution."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "what’s strong:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-9",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**clarity & predictability**: by tying fees to a subscription, you remove the black hole of hourly billing. clients love predictability, and so does your cash flow."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-7",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**focus on tools**: using linear for transparency and slack for real-time communication eliminates the chaos of email or scattered messages. stripe ties it all up with a financial bow."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-8",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**value without overhead**: the pitch of getting design and dev output without the hassle of hiring a team or wrangling freelancers is a solid hook."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-10",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "what might unravel:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-15",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-11",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**“unlimited” is a double-edged sword**: people hear \"unlimited\" and often lose touch with reality. managing the balance between what clients want and what you can deliver (at scale) is a potential minefield."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-12",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**scaling pains**: as demand grows, ensuring quality without overloading your team could be tricky. your concurrency caps are a smart safeguard, but there’s a fine line between protecting your bandwidth and frustrating clients with delays."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-13",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**overreliance on tools**: tools like slack and linear are only as good as the discipline behind them. if either you or your clients fail to keep them updated, the system falls apart."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-14",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**scope creep**: big tasks masquerading as small ones will need policing. a clear, shared understanding of what counts as “small,” “moderate,” or “large” work is non-negotiable."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-16",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "where this could shine:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-20",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-17",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "this model is ideal for startups or mid-size businesses that need regular output but lack the bandwidth for in-house teams."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-18",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "companies juggling multiple smaller projects could see this as a godsend, especially compared to piecing together talent from gig platforms or agencies."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-19",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "transparency and flexibility—done well—are your secret weapons. when clients feel like they’re in control, they’re more likely to trust the process."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-21",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "in summary:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "it’s promising—like a minimalist ikea shelf. sleek, practical, but demanding precise assembly. the transparency, subscription logic, and tiering are appealing, but execution will make or break it. done right, you could create a modern, scalable alternative to traditional design/dev agencies. just be prepared to occasionally remind clients that “unlimited” doesn’t mean infinite."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-23",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You said:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-24",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I like how this model leaves much of the responsiblity of setting pace & order of deliverables up to the client... what do you think? Is it better for the client to be the one to tell the client how long the entire thing will take, or have the client decide what should be done and in what order with the accountabillity of managing their requests strategically?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I imagine with this model it would give the client more liability and strategic control over the project's timeline."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-26",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "ChatGPT said:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "[](https://chatgpt.com/backend-api/content?id=file-wKWfHpqD9X0XXAwedeFQH7er&gizmo_id=g-wbfoUANvp&ts=482133&p=gpp&sig=db63631293766a1ba3ba7531eb7c5e7231e68c5290b453a94624d6c3b4159049&v=0)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "you’re absolutely right—this model flips the traditional dynamic. instead of you being the all-knowing oracle dictating timelines, it hands the reins to the client. they get to prioritize, strategize, and essentially \"own\" the pacing of their project. that shift has pros and cons, depending on the kind of client you’re dealing with."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-29",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "why it works:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-30",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **strategic empowerment**: clients who know their goals and have a clear vision will thrive here. they can prioritize based on what they need most urgently, which aligns the work directly with their business objectives."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-31",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **accountability shift**: by making them responsible for the queue, you’re protecting yourself from blame if things take longer. it’s their strategy, their choices."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-32",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **collaboration, not dependency**: clients aren’t passively waiting for updates—they’re actively involved in decision-making, which fosters a sense of partnership rather than a traditional client-provider dynamic."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-33",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. **flexibility for you**: you focus on delivering tasks within agreed-upon parameters rather than constantly renegotiating timelines for an entire project. it keeps your team more agile and reduces bottlenecks."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-34",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "potential pitfalls:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-35",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **clients can mismanage**: not all clients are good at strategizing or understanding task complexity. some might overload the queue with low-priority tasks or misjudge how long something will take, creating frustration."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-36",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **shifting blame**: while this model puts more liability on the client, it can still backfire if they mismanage their requests and blame you for not meeting their expectations."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **scope ambiguity**: if clients aren’t clear on what’s involved in certain tasks, they might underestimate their complexity, which could lead to delays or strained communication."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-38",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "balancing control:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-39",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "a middle ground could be helpful—some light guardrails to steer clients without micromanaging:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-43",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-40",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**offer guidance**: during onboarding, help clients understand how to prioritize effectively. maybe provide examples of “smart” task ordering versus chaotic ones."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-41",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**shared accountability**: clients decide the order, but you’re transparent about how their choices affect the timeline. this avoids surprises."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-42",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**optional strategy check-ins**: for clients who feel overwhelmed or unsure, you could offer periodic reviews of their queue to help them optimize."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-44",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "is this better?:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-45",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "for the right clients—absolutely. it’s empowering, transparent, and efficient. but for clients who lack the skills or bandwidth to manage their own priorities, it might feel overwhelming. in those cases, you’d need to either step in with more direction or adjust their expectations about how much hand-holding they’ll get."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-46",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "ultimately, the real win here is alignment. if the client takes ownership of their priorities and timeline, they’re more likely to feel satisfied with the process—even if things don’t move as fast as they’d hoped. it’s their strategy, their pacing, their outcome. there’s a kind of freedom in that—for both sides."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-47",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You said:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-48",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Maybe during onboarding we could give the client the option of deciding whether they want to be in control of the project mgmt and just have turtle deliver the work, or have turtle both manage the project and deliver the work... maybe we can make it cheaper for the client if they are the ones who are handling the project mgmt. what do you think?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-49",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "ChatGPT said:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-50",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "[](https://chatgpt.com/backend-api/content?id=file-wKWfHpqD9X0XXAwedeFQH7er&gizmo_id=g-wbfoUANvp&ts=482133&p=gpp&sig=db63631293766a1ba3ba7531eb7c5e7231e68c5290b453a94624d6c3b4159049&v=0)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-51",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "giving clients the option to choose their level of involvement is smart—it adds flexibility and caters to different types of clients. some thrive on control and want to oversee the details, while others just want the work done with minimal input. offering a cheaper option for clients who handle their own project management could also incentivize those who are confident in their ability to organize and prioritize."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-52",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "why this makes sense:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-53",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **tailored experience**: clients get to choose what works best for them. hands-on clients will feel empowered, while hands-off clients will feel relieved."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-54",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **cost alignment**: clients who take on more responsibility (project management) are saving you time and effort, so offering a discount aligns with the reduced workload on your side."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-55",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **clarity of roles**: having these two options clearly defined upfront sets expectations and minimizes misunderstandings later. if the client chooses to manage, it’s on them to keep things running smoothly."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-56",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "implementation ideas:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-57",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **tiered onboarding**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-58",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **self-managed tier**: during onboarding, you guide them on how to use the tools (linear, slack), prioritize tasks, and set realistic expectations for turnarounds. they own the queue and the pacing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-59",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **fully-managed tier**: your team takes charge of not just delivering but also planning and prioritizing. you regularly communicate progress and manage the client’s backlog to keep everything on track."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-60",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **pricing structure**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-61",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **self-managed**: lower monthly fee, reflecting the reduced labor on your end."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-62",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **fully-managed**: higher monthly fee, with the extra cost covering the project management overhead."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-63",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **clear boundaries**: for self-managed clients, it’s crucial to define what \"management\" entails. for example:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-64",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- you deliver according to the queue, but you’re not responsible for missed deadlines caused by poor prioritization."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-65",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- if they need project management help mid-subscription, you could charge extra or require them to upgrade to the fully-managed tier."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-66",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "potential challenges:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-67",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **mismanagement risks**: self-managed clients who underestimate the complexity of tasks or don’t prioritize effectively might struggle—and could turn their frustration on you. proactive communication and a solid onboarding process can mitigate this."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-68",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **scope creep for fully-managed clients**: taking on project management adds complexity for your team. you’ll need systems in place to handle this extra layer without it derailing your delivery pace."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-69",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **perceived value differences**: some clients might see the lower price for self-management and wonder why they’re paying extra for fully-managed, even if it’s justified."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-70",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "messaging to clients:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-71",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "frame it as empowering them to choose the relationship that best fits their needs:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-74",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-72",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**self-managed**: “you’re in control—you prioritize, we deliver. perfect for clients who like to manage their own workflows.”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-73",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**fully-managed**: “let us take the wheel—we’ll handle the planning, prioritization, and delivery so you can focus on your business.”"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-75",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "final thought:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-76",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "this approach is a win-win if handled well. clients who value autonomy can save money, while those who prefer to offload the project management entirely are willing to pay for the convenience. it also positions you as flexible and client-focused, which only strengthens the appeal of the subscription model. just make sure you’ve got clear processes and communication to support both tiers without spreading yourself thin."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-77",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You said:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-78",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "maybe we could offer a suggested SOW breaking down the timeline and phases free of charge even if they pick the self-managed option... that way it takes away some of the mental load while giving them the autonomy to use their own methods"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-79",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "ChatGPT said:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-80",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "[](https://chatgpt.com/backend-api/content?id=file-wKWfHpqD9X0XXAwedeFQH7er&gizmo_id=g-wbfoUANvp&ts=482133&p=gpp&sig=db63631293766a1ba3ba7531eb7c5e7231e68c5290b453a94624d6c3b4159049&v=0)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-81",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "that’s a brilliant way to strike a balance. offering a **suggested scope of work (SOW)** as part of onboarding is a thoughtful touch—it provides guidance without stepping on their autonomy. it shows you’re invested in their success even if they’re choosing the self-managed route, and it reduces the likelihood of them getting overwhelmed or mismanaging their project."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-82",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "why this works:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-83",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **removes friction**: a suggested SOW gives clients a clear starting point, easing the burden of figuring everything out themselves while still leaving them in control."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-84",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **guides expectations**: it subtly aligns their expectations with what’s realistic. they can see how long tasks typically take and what kind of pacing makes sense, reducing frustration later."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-85",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **value-add**: even at the self-managed tier, they get a taste of your strategic thinking, which reinforces trust and satisfaction."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-86",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. **less risk for you**: by giving them a roadmap, you lower the chances of them mismanaging priorities or timelines, which could lead to friction or dissatisfaction."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-87",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "what a suggested SOW could include:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-88",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **phases or milestones**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-89",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- phase 1: foundational tasks (e.g., research, initial designs, setup)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-90",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- phase 2: iterative work (e.g., core features, feedback cycles)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-91",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- phase 3: refinement and deployment (e.g., polishing, final delivery)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-92",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **task prioritization**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-93",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- an outline of suggested task categories and their order of importance (e.g., start with high-impact deliverables, defer low-priority tasks)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-94",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **estimated timelines**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-95",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- realistic turnaround times for task categories (e.g., \"branding assets: 3–5 days,\" \"new feature dev: 1–2 weeks\")."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-96",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. **strategic tips**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-97",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- advice on how to group or sequence tasks for maximum efficiency (e.g., “focus on MVP first before moving to edge-case features”)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-98",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "5. **clear disclaimers**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-99",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- a note that this is a suggested plan and may shift based on their priorities or how tasks evolve."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-100",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "positioning this:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-101",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "when presenting the SOW, emphasize that it’s a **baseline roadmap**, not a rigid plan:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-104",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-102",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "“this is a suggested plan to help you hit the ground running. it’s fully customizable, and you’re free to adjust it as you see fit.”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-103",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "“think of it as a guide to help you get the most out of your subscription while keeping things efficient.”"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-105",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "potential perks:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-109",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-106",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**enhanced client trust**: it signals that you’re invested in their project’s success, even if they’re managing it themselves."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-107",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**reduced friction down the line**: by preemptively setting expectations, you’ll field fewer complaints or misunderstandings about timing and priorities."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-108",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**optional upgrades**: if they see the value in your strategic input through the SOW, they might reconsider and opt for the fully-managed tier."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-110",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "final thought:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-111",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "a free suggested SOW is like handing over a map—you’re helping them navigate the project confidently while leaving the steering wheel in their hands. it’s a low-effort, high-impact way to make the self-managed option more attractive while protecting the quality of the process for both sides. it also reinforces the idea that even at the lower tier, you’re more than just executors—you’re strategic partners."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-112",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You said:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-113",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "what if we offer a structured map of the deliverables in no particular order for free (assuming we've had an in-depth discussion of the project and understand the scope in full), and provide the option for the client to manage the order that they are required vs turtle labs managing the timeline themselves?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-114",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "If we have not had an in-depth discovery call about the full project scope, then maybe the entire process can be hands-off and meeting-free (ideally), and we just deliver the work as it comes in regardless of whether we know what the final product or overall telos of the project is"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-115",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "ChatGPT said:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-116",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "[](https://chatgpt.com/backend-api/content?id=file-wKWfHpqD9X0XXAwedeFQH7er&gizmo_id=g-wbfoUANvp&ts=482133&p=gpp&sig=db63631293766a1ba3ba7531eb7c5e7231e68c5290b453a94624d6c3b4159049&v=0)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-117",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "this approach strikes a great balance between flexibility and structure, catering to both hands-on and hands-off clients. it respects different client preferences while keeping the process efficient and adaptable for your team."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-118",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "the structured map approach:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-119",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **post-discovery call**: if you’ve had an in-depth discussion about the project:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-120",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- provide a **deliverables map**: a detailed list of tasks or phases broken down into logical categories (design, dev, consulting, etc.)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-121",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- no strict order: let the client decide the sequence, aligning the flow with their priorities and needs."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-122",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- optional project management: give the client the choice to either manage the timeline themselves or hand it over to turtle labs for a more curated process."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-123",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **no discovery call**: if the client opts to skip deep onboarding:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-124",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **hands-off execution**: you focus purely on delivering tasks as they come in, with no expectation of understanding the broader project scope."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-125",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **minimal overhead**: clients submit tasks one at a time or in batches, and your team delivers without worrying about how the pieces fit into a larger picture."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-126",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "benefits of this approach:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-127",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **flexibility for clients**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-128",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- structured but not rigid: clients with a clear vision can manage the order of deliverables themselves, while others can rely on you to steer the timeline."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-129",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- no-pressure onboarding: clients who want to avoid lengthy calls or deep planning sessions can jump straight into action."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-130",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **streamlined for your team**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-131",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- discovery-based projects get a solid foundation, reducing guesswork and potential rework."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-132",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- hands-off projects minimize client interactions, allowing your team to focus purely on execution."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-133",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **reduced friction**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-134",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- the structured map eliminates ambiguity for clients who manage their own timelines."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-135",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- the hands-off option keeps things efficient for clients who don’t want to micromanage or strategize."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-136",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "communication & framing:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-138",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-137",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**structured map**:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-139",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- “after our discovery call, we’ll provide you with a roadmap of deliverables based on what we’ve discussed. you’re free to decide the order or let us handle the timeline for you.”"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-141",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-140",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**hands-off option**:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-142",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- “if you’d prefer to skip a full discovery session, we’ll deliver tasks as they come in, focusing on what’s next in the queue. this approach is great for clients who want to dive right in without a detailed upfront plan.”"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-143",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "potential challenges & solutions:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-144",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **clients misunderstanding hands-off limitations**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-145",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- clarify that hands-off doesn’t include strategic oversight or ensuring a cohesive final product. emphasize that you’re delivering discrete tasks based on their instructions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-146",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- example: “with the hands-off option, we’ll execute each request as it comes in. this is ideal for clients who already have a clear vision or are focusing on individual tasks rather than the full scope.”"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-147",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **balancing the structured map’s flexibility**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-148",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- for clients managing their own timeline, ensure they understand the implications of their choices. e.g., “re-prioritizing tasks may extend the overall timeline, but we’ll stay agile to accommodate your needs.”"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-149",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **time investment for discovery calls**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-150",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- limit the scope of the call to stay efficient. you’re not planning every detail—just enough to understand the big picture and provide a useful deliverables map."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-151",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "why this works:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-152",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "it caters to a spectrum of clients:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-156",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-153",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**hands-on clients** feel empowered to manage their own priorities."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-154",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**hands-off clients** appreciate the efficiency and minimal friction."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-155",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "it also lets turtle labs maintain operational efficiency while delivering high-value guidance where needed. it’s a thoughtful, modular approach that scales well and minimizes unnecessary complexity."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}